{"records":[{"id":"9x47wzy8x7","title":"A study of \"Genome-wide CRISPR screens reveal host factors critical for SARS-CoV-2 infection\" by Wei et al. Cell 2020","description":"Identification of host genes essential for SARS-CoV-2 infection may reveal novel therapeutic targets and inform our understanding of COVID-19 pathogenesis. Here, we performed genome-wide CRISPR screens in Vero-E6 cells with SARS-CoV-2, MERS-CoV, bat coronavirus HKU5 expressing the SARS-CoV-1 spike, and VSV expressing the SARS-CoV-2 spike. Together this identifies potential therapeutic targets for SARS-CoV-2 and reveals SARS-lineage specific and pan-coronavirus host factors that regulate susceptibility to highly pathogenic coronaviruses.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-10-15T21:29:14.06Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9x47wzy8x7","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9x47wzy8x7"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Craig","last_name":"Wilen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR","Middle East Respiratory Syndrome-Related Coronavirus","Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"hfbhym45fz","title":"CRISPR screening reveals a requirement for ribosome recycling in efficient SARS-CoV-2 programmed ribosomal frameshifting and viral replication. Rehfeld et al.","description":"Supplemental Table S1. Results of SARS-CoV-2 programmed ribosomal frameshifting genome-wide CRISPR screens (MAGeCK analysis).\nSupplemental Table S2. Oligonucleotides.\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-01-19T12:17:58.922Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/hfbhym45fz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/hfbhym45fz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Joshua","last_name":"Mendell","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Frederick","last_name":"Rehfeld","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/0003xa228","name":"Cancer Prevention and Research Institute of Texas","grant_id":"RP220309"},{"id":"https://ror.org/00np6vq88","name":"Welch Foundation","grant_id":"I-1961-20210327"},{"id":"https://ror.org/006w34k90","name":"Howard Hughes Medical Institute","grant_id":null}],"categories":["Oligonucleotide","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"8gj97c4kgv","title":"Genome-wide mapping of SARS-CoV-2 RNA structures identifies therapeutically-relevant elements","description":"This dataset included the files for both benchmark and the structured segment in the SARS-CoV-2 genome described in the article 'Genome-wide mapping of SARS-CoV-2 RNA structures identifies therapeutically-relevant elements'.  The description of the methods followed is available in the article in detail. Each directory and sub-directory has individual descriptions.\nThe article is available at https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkaa1053 \n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-11-04T18:06:47.731Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/8gj97c4kgv","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/8gj97c4kgv"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Ilaria","last_name":"Manfredonia","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Chandran","last_name":"Nithin","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Almudena","last_name":"Ponce-Salvatierra","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Pritha","last_name":"Ghosh","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tomasz K","last_name":"Wirecki","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tycho","last_name":"Marinus","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Eric J","last_name":"Snider","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Natacha S","last_name":"Ogando","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Martijn J","last_name":" van Hemert","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Janusz M","last_name":" Bujnicki","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Danny","last_name":"Incarnato","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["RNA","Computational Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"gcdpsxd6d5","title":"RNAi screening using HK-2 cells: insights into the roles of soluble ACE2 in SARS-CoV-2 infection. Yeung et al","description":"Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) can cause acute respiratory disease and multiorgan failure. Finding human host factors that are essential for SARS-CoV-2 infection could facilitate the formulation of treatment strategies. Using a human kidney cell line—HK-2—that is highly susceptible to SARS-CoV-2, we performed a genome-wide RNAi screening and identified virus dependency factors (VDFs), which play regulatory roles in biological pathways linked to clinical manifestations of SARS-CoV-2 infection. Importantly, we discovered an overlooked role of a secretory form of SARS-CoV-2 receptor, soluble angiotensin converting enzyme 2 (sACE2), in SARS-CoV-2 infection. Further investigations revealed that SARS-CoV-2 exploits receptor-mediated endocytosis through interaction between its spike with sACE2 or sACE2-vasopressin via AT1 or AVPR1B, respectively. Our identification of new VDFs and the regulatory effect of sACE2 on SARS-CoV-2 infection shed new insights into pathogenesis and cell entry mechanism of SARS-CoV-2 as well as potential treatment strategies for COVID-19.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-02-22T23:41:07.557Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/gcdpsxd6d5","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/gcdpsxd6d5"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Man Lung","last_name":"Yeung","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Screening","RNA Knockdown"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"72tr8jj8y4","title":"RNAi screening using HK-2 cells: insights into the roles of soluble ACE2 in SARS-CoV-2 infection. Yeung et al","description":"Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) can cause acute respiratory disease and multiorgan failure. Finding human host factors that are essential for SARS-CoV-2 infection could facilitate the formulation of treatment strategies. Using a human kidney cell line—HK-2—that is highly susceptible to SARS-CoV-2, we performed a genome-wide RNAi screening and identified virus dependency factors (VDFs), which play regulatory roles in biological pathways linked to clinical manifestations of SARS-CoV-2 infection. Importantly, we discovered an overlooked role of a secretory form of SARS-CoV-2 receptor, soluble angiotensin converting enzyme 2 (sACE2), in SARS-CoV-2 infection. Further investigations revealed that SARS-CoV-2 exploits receptor-mediated endocytosis through interaction between its spike with sACE2 or sACE2-vasopressin via AT1 or AVPR1B, respectively. Our identification of new VDFs and the regulatory effect of sACE2 on SARS-CoV-2 infection shed new insights into pathogenesis and cell entry mechanism of SARS-CoV-2 as well as potential treatment strategies for COVID-19.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-02-22T23:48:03.555Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/72tr8jj8y4","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/72tr8jj8y4"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Man Lung","last_name":"Yeung","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Vasopressin","Screening","RNA Knockdown","Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"f7btcr6x6d","title":"A non-canonical function of glutathione to suppress ferroptosis via FSP1","description":"Whole genome-wide CRISPR KO screen","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-10-02T11:41:52.925Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/f7btcr6x6d","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/f7btcr6x6d"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"BO","last_name":"CHU","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"42sxkx9sdb","title":"Synthetic lethality-based prediction of anti-SARS-CoV-2 targets. Pal et al","description":"Supplementary data for the paper: \"Synthetic lethality-based prediction of anti-SARS-CoV-2 targets\". \nTable S1: Enriched Reactome pathways for DE gene sets (FDR<0.1). (Related to STAR Methods and Figure 2).\nTable S2: List of synthetic lethal pairs in each of the transcriptomic dataset used in this study and the list of unified 454 SL/SDL partner genes. (Related to STAR Methods and Figure 1).\nTable S3: List of 140 candidate targets and three subsets comprising known drug targets, hub SL/SDL partner genes when each one of them are paired up with multiple DE genes and genes with enriched Reactome pathways.  Pathway enrichment analysis (FDR <0.1) for SL/SDL partner genes, DE genes and combination pathway enrichment analysis for DE gene-SL/SDL partner gene pairs for 140 candidates. List of 135 candidates overlapping with genome-wide siRNA screen. (Related to STAR Methods and Figure 1 and 2).\nTable S4: Targeted siRNA screen results for selected 26 targets and annotation of 26 candidate targets with reference to SARS-CoV-2 or any other virus in the literature. (Related to STAR Methods and Figure 3).\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-04-19T18:44:35.774Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/42sxkx9sdb","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/42sxkx9sdb"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lipika","last_name":"R. Pal","orcid":"0000-0002-3390-110X"},{"first_name":"Kuoyuan","last_name":"Cheng","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nishanth Ulhas","last_name":"Nair","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Laura","last_name":"Martin-Sancho","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sanju","last_name":"Sinha","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Yuan","last_name":"Pu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Laura","last_name":"Riva","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Yin","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Fiorella","last_name":"Schischlik","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Joo Sang","last_name":"Lee","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sumit K.","last_name":"Chanda","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Eytan","last_name":"Ruppin","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Transcriptome","Drug","Antiviral Therapy","CRISPR/Cas9","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"9rc2n4bkmv","title":"Functional interrogation of a SARS-CoV-2 host protein interactome identifies unique and shared coronavirus host factors. Hoffmann et al.","description":"The ongoing SARS-CoV-2 pandemic has devastated the global economy and claimed more than one million lives, presenting an urgent global health crisis. To identify host factors required for infection by SARS-CoV-2 and seasonal coronaviruses, we designed a focused high-coverage CRISPR-Cas9 library targeting 332 members of a recently published SARS-CoV-2 protein interactome. We leveraged the compact nature of this library to systematically screen SARS-CoV-2 at two physiologically relevant temperatures (33 ºC and 37 ºC) along with three related coronaviruses (HCoV-229E, HCoV-NL63, and HCoV-OC43), allowing us to probe this interactome at a much higher resolution relative to genome scale studies. This approach yielded several new insights, including unexpected virus-specific differences in Rab GTPase requirements and GPI anchor biosynthesis, as well as identification of multiple pan-coronavirus factors involved in cholesterol homeostasis. This coronavirus essentiality catalog could inform ongoing drug development efforts aimed at intercepting and treating COVID-19, and help prepare for future coronavirus outbreaks.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-11-25T19:01:19.445Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9rc2n4bkmv","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9rc2n4bkmv"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"JT","last_name":"Poirier","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Coronavirus","Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"96jwcyxgn6","title":"An Airway Organoid-Based Screen Identifies a Role for the HIF1α-Glycolysis Axis in SARS-CoV-2 Infection ","description":"SARS-CoV-2 causes the COVID-19 pandemic. It is urgent to develop disease models to dissect mechanisms regulating SARS-CoV-2 infection. Here, we derive airway organoids from human pluripotent stem cells (hPSC-AOs). The hPSC-AOs, particularly ciliated-like cells, are permissive to SARS-CoV-2 infection. Using this platform, we perform a high content screen and identify GW6471, which blocks SARS-CoV-2 infection. GW6471 can also block infection of the B.1.351 SARS-CoV-2 variant. RNA-seq analysis suggests that GW6471 blocks SARS-CoV-2 infection at least in part by inhibiting HIF1α, which is further validated by chemical inhibitor and genetic perturbation targeting HIF1α. Metabolic profiling identifies decreased rates of glycolysis upon GW6471 treatment, consistent with transcriptome profiling. Finally, xanthohumol, 5-(Tetradecyloxy)-2-furoic acid, and ND-646, three compounds that suppress fatty acid biosynthesis, also block SARS-CoV-2 infection. Together, a high content screen coupled with transcriptome and metabolic profiling reveals a key role of the HIF1α-glycolysis axis in mediating SARS-CoV-2 infection of human airway epithelium.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-10-08T10:41:17.03Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/96jwcyxgn6","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/96jwcyxgn6"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Shuibing","last_name":"Chen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Supplemental Irrigation"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ygj2yfj9k5","title":"A study of structural characterization of SARS-CoV-2. Sun et al","description":"The supplementary table S1-S7 of our paper entitled \"In vivo structural characterization of the SARS-CoV-2 RNA genome identifies host proteins vulnerable to repurposed drugs\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-11-16T16:04:56.181Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ygj2yfj9k5","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ygj2yfj9k5"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"LEI","last_name":"SUN","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Pan","last_name":"Li","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xiaohui","last_name":"Ju","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jian","last_name":"Rao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["RNA Structure","Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":104639,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":117,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":104639,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":104274,"restricted":51,"embargoed":314},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":1665},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":524},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Centre","count":384},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":335},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":313},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":307},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":301},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":290},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":217},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":213}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":102401},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1664},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":140},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":108},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":59},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f84e575e4","name":"Digital Commons Data@Becker","count":58},{"id":"72c28c45-627f-446b-8a48-af7c0a51a357","name":"Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore","count":38},{"id":"b121dfec-bb51-4f19-a2f6-bc9ce0197286","name":"Babeș-Bolyai University","count":31},{"id":"f2ed6517-7fb4-4e02-8cef-95e75e9f0c9d","name":"Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University","count":25},{"id":"5f1edf21-7948-4d82-894f-c0ed4b1e8f52","name":"Teesside University","count":24}],"top_institutions_stats":[{"id":"0ad97c43-5173-56e6-bbe6-46dad5323862","name":"Daffodil International University","count":386},{"id":"55ba66b2-f276-5204-a3d8-acfa499794e0","name":"The University of Manchester","count":297},{"id":"f58d7a83-6efa-5d8a-a6c2-b9e78ee14783","name":"Maharishi Markandeshwar Institute of Physiotherapy and Rehabilitation","count":255},{"id":"3bfef41a-d03e-5722-bd55-dd245235fa78","name":"Bina Nusantara University","count":242},{"id":"9d63ad1d-c391-5c35-a12e-cafe17017098","name":"Universidad Autonoma de Madrid","count":234}]}}